            "rob_routing_evidence_json": "[\"A retrospective cohort analysis was performed using the TriNetX Research Network, a federated electronic health record platform containing data from 112 healthcare organizations across five countries, encompassing record\", \"Subjects aged 50 years or older were assigned to cohorts based on initiation of GLP-1 RA or OWL pharmacotherapy, as previously described.\", \"Outcomes were assessed using Cox proportional hazards models.\"]",
            "rob_attempted": true,
            "assessment_status": "completed",
            "rob_skip_or_failure_reason": "",
            "overall_risk_of_bias": "moderate",
            "overall_reason": "Overall risk of bias is judged moderate for incident any AMD. The retrospective active-comparator new-user cohort used extensive propensity-score matching on demographics, BMI, hemoglobin A1c, AMD risk factors, comorbidities, ophthalmology access, and proxies for social determinants of health, with post-matching SMDs reported as <0.20, and used time-to-event analysis with censoring. However, as an observational EHR study it remains vulnerable to residual and unmeasured confounding, incomplete or differential AMD ascertainment through diagnostic codes, informative loss of EHR follow-up, and unknown adherence or medication switching. Negative-control analyses and active comparator design reduce but do not eliminate these concerns.",
