            "overall_risk_of_bias": "serious",
            "overall_reason": "Overall risk of bias is judged serious for the review-relevant result on incident any AMD. The study was a claims-based matched case-control analysis in diabetic patients, and the review-relevant GLP-1 receptor agonist exposure was not isolated: exenatide was combined with sitagliptin and pramlintide as \u201cother diabetic medications.\u201d Important confounding by diabetes severity, treatment indication, glycemic control, obesity, healthcare utilization, and other AMD risk factors may remain despite multivariable adjustment for known AMD risk factors. Exposure and outcome ascertainment relied on administrative claims, and medication use was assessed retrospectively before the index AMD/control visit. These issues are sufficient for a serious overall judgment, although the very large sample and reporting of several medication categories reduce concern for some domains.",
