                "overall_reason": "Overall risk of bias is serious for incident any AMD. The study used a large matched retrospective active-comparator cohort and time-to-event methods, but important concerns remain: exposure groups were selected after demonstrating at least six months of therapy, follow-up was substantially shorter in the GLP-1RA group, HbA1c was differentially missing and not adjusted for, and AMD ascertainment was based on routine structured data without imaging validation in the supplied text. These issues could plausibly bias the estimated association in an unpredictable direction, although differential follow-up and healthcare-contact patterns could particularly affect detection of AMD.",
