                "overall_reason": "For incident nonneovascular AMD, the result comes from a retrospective EHR-based propensity-matched cohort rather than random allocation. Active comparator matching reduced measured baseline imbalance, but substantial potential remains for confounding by indication, metabolic/diabetes severity, ophthalmic risk factors, and healthcare-use patterns; the text also reports residual HbA1c imbalance in the GLP-1RA versus lipid-lowering comparison. Selection into analyses requiring ophthalmology follow-up and documented medication use over 1, 2, or 3 years may also have introduced post-index selection bias. Outcome ascertainment relied on routine diagnosis documentation rather than standardized masked retinal imaging assessment. These concerns make the overall risk of bias serious, though not clearly critical based on the supplied text.",
