              "overall_risk_of_bias": "serious",
              "overall_reason": "Overall risk of bias is serious for incident neovascular/exudative AMD. In addition to the non-randomized matched cohort limitations, the nAMD result is particularly vulnerable to outcome misclassification and analytic instability: the main multivariable Cox model was null, while sequential follow-up-accounting models produced a protective association. Post-index anti-VEGF treatment rates were nearly identical between groups, which is useful as a validation check but also highlights uncertainty in the coded nAMD phenotype. Bias direction is unpredictable."
