              "overall_reason": "Overall risk of bias is judged serious for the incident exudative/neovascular AMD result. The active-comparator new-user design and matching reduce bias, and the exudative AMD subtype was defined using a prespecified ICD-10-CM code. Nevertheless, the result remains vulnerable to serious residual confounding from baseline metabolic imbalance, with aggregate data limiting further adjustment. Additional concerns include differential follow-up, unavailable adherence and discontinuation information, incomplete missing-data reporting, and possible EHR coding or surveillance-related outcome misclassification."
