              "overall_reason": "Overall risk of bias was judged serious for conversion from nonexudative AMD to exudative/neovascular AMD. This secondary progression analysis was based on a much smaller baseline nonexudative AMD cohort, used code-based AMD classification, and had residual confounding concerns that are particularly important for progression outcomes, including absence of detailed baseline AMD severity, retinal imaging, ophthalmic care intensity, and treatment persistence information."
