              "overall_risk_of_bias": "serious",
              "overall_reason": "Overall risk of bias is judged serious for the incident nonexudative AMD result. The study used a reasonably strong observational design with active-comparator new-user matching and prespecified subtype coding. However, substantial residual imbalance in BMI and HbA1c after matching, attenuation of AMD associations in glycemic sensitivity analyses, limitations of aggregate data, and possible unmeasured AMD risk and surveillance factors create serious confounding concerns. Additional moderate concerns arise from differential follow-up, unavailable adherence/discontinuation information, incomplete missing-data reporting, and code-based outcome measurement."
