              "overall_reason": "Overall risk of bias is serious for post-index anti-VEGF treatment. Anti-VEGF treatment is a more objectively recorded utilization outcome than diagnostic AMD codes, but the same non-randomized, post-initiation selection and differential follow-up concerns apply. In addition, anti-VEGF treatment is not specific to nAMD in a diabetic population and may reflect diabetic macular edema or other retinal disease, making interpretation as an AMD-related endpoint susceptible to confounding and outcome-context misclassification."
