              "allocation_unit": "not_applicable",
              "evidence": [
                "Using a retrospective cohort study design, the platform was queried using Current Procedural Technology (CPT) codes to generate 5 cohorts",
                "The TriNetX United States collaborative network of aggregated, de-identified EHR data from nearly 108 million patients and 62 contributing health care organizations, including academic and private practice centers, from",
                "Each cohort then was divided based on whether the patient was prescribed a GLP-1RA (dulaglutide, lixisenatide, albiglutide, exenatide, semaglutide, or liraglutide), metformin, a statin (fluvastatin, lovastatin, atorvasta"
              ],
              "reason": "The study retrospectively compared medication-use cohorts to estimate effects of GLP-1RA treatment on ocular outcomes."
