          "rob_input_excerpt": "## Focused source excerpt 1\nUsed for: outcome_02: Incident exudative or neovascular age-related macular degeneration\n\n## 277 **Figure Legends** \n\n## 278 \n\n279 Figure 2: Forest Plot for the Active Comparator New-User Cohort Analysis. Hazard ratio (HR) 280 and 95% confidence interval (CI) estimates for the risk of neovascular age-related macular 281 degeneration (NVAMD) while on-treatment with a 2nd line type 2 diabetes (T2D) medication 282 comparing between semaglutide and other GLP-1RAs (dulaglutide, exenatide) and non-GLP283 1RA medications (empagliflozin, sitagliptin, and glipizide). Only results from databases and 284 comparisons that passed study diagnostics are provided, as well as the meta-analytic 285 estimates.* The total number of patients in each comparison is shown. The panel on the left 286 shows the results using the NVAMD-C definition that uses condition codes alone, while the 287 panel on the right uses the NVAMD-CP definition that uses condition and procedure codes. \n\n303 \n\n304 \n\n305 \n\n306 \n\n307 \n\n308 \n\n309 \n\n310 \n\n*Databases that have 0 cases of NVAMD are unable to produce hazard ratio (HR) estimates but still contribute to the meta-analytic estimate Abbreviations:",
