          "rob_input_excerpt": "## Focused source excerpt 1\nUsed for: outcome_01: Incident any age-related macular degeneration; outcome_02: Incident exudative or neovascular age-related macular degeneration; outcome_05: Incident nonexudative age-related macular degeneration; study design/RoB\n\n## Statistical Analysis \n\nThe primary outcome was the relative risk (RR) for nonexudative AMD development after yearly drug duration intervals of GLP1RA use compared with the other diabetic medication controls: SGLT-2i, metformin, or insulin. Drug durations were calculated using drug prescription EHR data. If the stop date was scheduled to be after the day of the data pull, the date of the data pull was used as the stop date. A new AMD diagnosis after each year of medication use was used for RR calculation. The RR and 95% confidence intervals (CIs) were calculated using multivariable logistic regression models controlling for age at starting the study drug, sex, race, smoking status (current, former, or never smoker), and baseline hemoglobin A1C (HbA1C) percentage. The data for this analysis were pulled on March 27, 2025. Relative risk was measured for each of the comparisons at 1-year intervals up to 3 years of drug durati",
