          "rob_input_excerpt": "## Focused source excerpt 1\nUsed for: outcome_01: Incident any age-related macular degeneration; outcome_02: Incident exudative or neovascular age-related macular degeneration; outcome_03: Conversion from nonexudative AMD to exudative or neovascular AMD; outcome_04: Progression to advanced or atrophic nonexudative AMD; outcome_05: Incident nonexudative age-related macular degeneration; outcome_06: Combined progression to advanced AMD; study design/RoB\n\n## Results \n\n## Study Population \n\nA total of 5,803,327 patients with T2DM and no history of AMD met inclusion criteria and were assigned to one of two cohorts based upon GLP1RA use status. After propensity score matching, 600,816 patients with T2DM who received GLP1RA therapy were matched to an identical number who received non\u2013GLP-1RA-based therapy. Demographic and baseline clinical characteristics of the propensity score-matched cohorts with no pre-existing AMD are summarized in Table 1. Comparison of demographic characteristics between the two groups indicated that the average age was 58.0 (612.8) years and 57.1 (614.3) years in the GLP-1RA and non\u2013 \n\nGLP-1RA cohorts, respectively (P , 0.001; standard difference (StdDiff) 0.065).",
