          "rob_input_excerpt": "## Focused source excerpt 1\nUsed for: outcome_02: Incident exudative or neovascular age-related macular degeneration; study design/RoB\n\nThe study adhered to the Strengthening the Reporting of Observational Studies in Epidemiology (STROBE) reporting guidelines and received approval from the University of Toronto Research Ethics Board (REB 45832). \n\n## Data Sources \n\nThis population-based cohort study was conducted in Ontario, Canada, using linked administrative health and demographic data. Health records were accessed through ICES (formerly the Institute for Clinical Evaluative Sciences), an independent, nonprofit research institute. Under Ontario\u2019s healthinformationprivacylaw,ICESisauthorizedtocollectand analyze health care and demographic data without individual consent for the purposes of health system evaluation and improvement. We used multiple ICES datasets, each marked with a common encrypted identifier (ICES key number), to facilitate linkage across datasets. The Ontario Health Insurance Plan (OHIP)recordsprovidedbillinginformationforpatientswhoreceived in-office or in-hospital care using specific _International Classification of Diseases, Ninth Revision_ ( _ICD-9_ ) or _Int",
